    "Description": "This is a kernel live patch module which can be loaded by the kpatch command line utility to modify the code of a running kernel.  This patch module is targeted for kernel-5.14.0-427.100.1.el9_4.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: netfilter: ebtables SNAT target writes to shared memory pages during ARP hardware address rewrite (CVE-2026-53266)\n\n* kernel: pppoe: reload header pointer after dev_hard_header() (CVE-2026-68121)\n\n* kernel: net: bridge: stop fast-leave after deleting a port group (CVE-2026-74480)\n\n* kernel: packet: use consistent hard_header_len in non-ring send paths (CVE-2026-74582)\n\n* kernel: xfrm: ah6: validate routing header segments_left (CVE-2026-80844)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
